  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Could you help me see how genes are connected in my sorghum heat-stress experiment?"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "What I understood you are asking for:\n1. \"how genes are connected in my sorghum heat-stress experiment\" -- available from PANDA, LIONESS-PANDA, OTTER, LIONESS-COEXPRESSION or BONOBO.\n\nSeveral registered methods fit this result; they differ in their modeling assumptions:\n\n- **LIONESS-COEXPRESSION** — LIONESS represents the cohort network through sample contributions: W_q = N*W_all - (N-1)*W_without_q, where N is the cohort size and the same base estimator is fitted with and without sample q. Needs expression matrix.\n- **COBRA** — COBRA models co-expression as a function of sample covariates through conditional covariance estimation. Needs expression matrix and sample covariate design matrix.\n\nBoth fit; to choose, tell me: (1) Do you need to separate or adjust co-expression for batch, site or other sample covariates? (co-expression must be separated or adjusted for batch, site or other covariates → COBRA; no sample covariates need to be separated or adjusted → LIONESS-COEXPRESSION)\n\nNo files were inspected and no analysis ran."
    }
  ],
